---------------------------------------------------------------------------
A note on authorship
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The code in this repository was written end to end by Claude Opus 5, an AI
model made by Anthropic, in a single session. A human specified the idea, set
the constraints, and reviewed the result, but did not write the code.

The copyright line above deliberately names no individual. In most
jurisdictions, material generated by an AI without human creative authorship
is not eligible for copyright, so naming a person as the author would be
inaccurate, and naming the model would assert a right it cannot hold. The MIT
terms are kept because they are what people expect from a tool like this, and
because any human-authored contributions made later are genuinely covered by
them.

If you would prefer to treat this as public domain, you may: the original
authors assert no rights over the AI-generated portions.
